{"comparisons":[],"failures":[],"frontier":[],"initial":{"alternatives":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and the circular’s fund-distribution context.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Describes additional features and restrictions; does not limit the gift control to these examples.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Describes standing-instruction services relevant to later marketing provisions.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Public campaigns are background, not an express public-only condition for the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Guaranteed-returns heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Identifies the separate statutory provision.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Explains the components of typical guaranteed returns, without defining every such return as a gift.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Conditional structured-product classification belongs to a separate control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Statutory advertisement prohibition and its exceptions are separate from the gift control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Offering-document and misleading-impression concerns supply context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies paragraph 3.11 as the selected control’s source.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Gift classification remains conditional; the gift control can apply independently of structured-product classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"Operative gift rule, fee-discount exception, and product or product-type connection.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Connects the two independent controls without prohibiting every additional return categorically.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u15"},{"reason":"Separate dealing-restrictions heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u16"},{"reason":"Examples of dealing restrictions outside the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Separate fairness and redemption requirements; full General Principle 1 remains an external dependency.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u18"},{"reason":"Separate dealing-frequency expectation; administrative flexibility is not a gift exception.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u19"},{"reason":"Separate marketing heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u20"},{"reason":"Separate misleading-advertising obligation referring to paragraph 2.3.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u21"},{"reason":"Separate advertising-guidelines requirement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u22"},{"reason":"Separate restrictions on risk-free and deposit-like advertising.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u23"},{"reason":"Monitoring and possible regulatory action; supplies no effective date or automatic sanction for the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u24"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u25"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u26"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u27"},{"reason":"Footnote supplies offering-document context; underlying Handbook provisions are not supplied in full.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u28"},{"reason":"Identifies the Code, including licensed and registered persons; does not supply its complete application provisions.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u29"},{"reason":"Identifies a materially relevant FAQ and its issue date, but its answer is absent.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u30"},{"reason":"Unspecified evolving supplements relate to advertising guidelines; their content is absent.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u31"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The selected control addresses distributors promoting a specific investment product or particular product type to a client. The circular defines distributors through SFC-authorised funds; its opening observations about licensed corporations do not establish that registered intermediaries are excluded. The full Code’s application beyond this circular remains unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u14","u29"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Neither gift nor discount of fees or charges is exhaustively defined. Guaranteed returns and other incentives may be gifts; classification is not automatic. Fund types and funds from particular fund houses expressly illustrate product-type links.","source_unit_ids":["u8","u13","u14"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The fee-discount parenthesis qualifies the gifts covered by paragraph 3.11, including the later linked-gift explanation. Section 103 authorisation or exemption is a separate exception and does not excuse a gift under paragraph 3.11.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u15"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The text presents 'should not' as a regulatory requirement, while 'may be considered' preserves uncertainty about incentive classification. It does not establish that every breach of this control is the statutory offence described separately.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u24"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The control concerns offering gifts in promotion, without requiring payment or completed investment. No commencement date, transition rule, or assessment date is supplied. The date 2010-09-30 identifies the referenced FAQ’s issue date, not this control’s commencement.","source_unit_ids":["u14","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The complete paragraph 3.11, Code application provisions and FAQ answer are absent. The packet’s external-authorities.23ec46 dependency has no supplied content or source hash. Separate SFO, Handbook and advertising requirements cannot be resolved by this selected control.","source_unit_ids":["u7","u10","u12","u18","u21","u22","u28","u29","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does paragraph 3.11 or the referenced FAQ distinguish a genuine retrospective fee rebate from a cash gift calculated by reference to fees?","What establishes a sufficient product-type link for a promotion spanning several product categories, including funds from particular fund houses?","What do the full Code application provisions establish about actors and products beyond the circular’s SFC-authorised-fund context?","Which version and effective date of paragraph 3.11 and its FAQ govern the offer being assessed?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The assessment concerns one identified promotional offer by an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds.","The result is a screen for the selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control only, evaluated when scope is true.","Gift, discount and product-link classifications must be supplied from evidence and judgment; unknown classifications remain unknown.","No independent requirement to prove actual investor distraction is added: the text states distraction as the purpose and rationale."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"u15"},{"quote":"3 The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"u30"}],"distinction":"The supported reading attaches the exception to qualifying fee discounts and reaches both individual-product and product-type promotions. For a concrete classification boundary, consider a cash payment after subscribing to funds from one fund house, equal to the subscription fee. If it genuinely reduces that fee, the selected screen passes; if it is a separate gift merely measured by the fee, it fails. The supplied text does not decide which classification applies, so these are unresolved applications rather than two asserted legal rules. By contrast, excluding all fund-house-wide promotions because no single fund is named is contradicted by the express example.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor making the assessed offer is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the circular’s distributor description.","name":"actor_is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed offer occurs in promoting an investment product or investment service involving such products to a client.","name":"promotion_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed promotion or offered benefit is connected to a specific investment product or particular product type, including a qualifying fund-type or fund-house link.","name":"qualifying_product_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed offer includes a benefit classified as a gift for paragraph 3.11; a guaranteed return or incentive is not automatically assigned this classification.","name":"gift_offered","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the express exception.","name":"qualifying_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(or (not gift_offered) qualifying_fee_discount)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and actor_is_distributor promotion_to_client qualifying_product_link)"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Does an after-payment refund legally reduce the relevant fees, or constitute a distinct promotional benefit?","Does the missing FAQ specify how indirect or mixed-product links are assessed?","Are there additional application provisions or exceptions in the complete paragraph 3.11?"],"statement":"For the selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control, an in-scope distributor should not offer a gift in a client promotion connected to a specific investment product or particular product type unless the benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges. The linked-product-type explanation carries the same exception. Structured-product classification and section 103 authorisation are separate issues. The strongest unresolved issue is classification of borderline rebates and incentives, which the retained text and absent FAQ do not settle.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: fee-discount exception and product connection"}]},"controlled-language":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and frames the circular around SFC-authorised funds.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Describes added features motivating the circular.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Describes standing-instruction services, not the selected gift control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Marketing background; does not impose a public-campaign limitation on u14.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Section heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Identifies a separate statutory control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Explains guaranteed-return arrangements without conclusively classifying them as gifts.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Possible structured-product classification is distinct from gift classification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Separate offence and statutory exceptions; these are not exceptions to u14.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Disclosure and misleading-impression concerns provide context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies paragraph 3.11 as the selected control's source.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Preserves uncertain gift classification and independence from structured-product classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"Principal text for the gift restriction, discount exception and product connection.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Fund-specific synthesis supports the contextual scope alternative while preserving separate legal controls.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u15"},{"reason":"Separate dealing-frequency heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u16"},{"reason":"Examples of redemption restrictions outside the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Separate fairness and redemption requirements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u18"},{"reason":"Separate best-endeavours requirement; its administrative qualification does not attach to gifts.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u19"},{"reason":"Separate marketing heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u20"},{"reason":"Separate misleading-advertising requirement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u21"},{"reason":"Separate advertising-guideline dependency.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u22"},{"reason":"Separate restrictions on risk and deposit comparisons.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u23"},{"reason":"Monitoring and possible regulatory action do not specify the selected control's sanctions or commencement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u24"},{"reason":"Departmental attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u25"},{"reason":"Divisional and institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u26"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u27"},{"reason":"Offering-document footnote; full Handbook requirements remain outside the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u28"},{"reason":"Names the Code and its licensed-or-registered population; does not by itself settle the circular's actor scope.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u29"},{"reason":"Identifies the dated FAQ supporting product-type linkage, but its answer is not supplied.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u30"},{"reason":"Unprovided evolving advertising guidance concerns the separate advertising provisions.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u31"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The circular defines distributors by distribution of SFC-authorised funds, while u14 restates a control using general investment-product language. The alternatives differ over whether this selected control reaches those distributors' promotions of other investment products. Neither imports the separate section 103 Hong Kong-public condition.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u10","u14","u15","u29"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Gift is not exhaustively defined. Additional returns and incentives may qualify, rather than necessarily qualifying. Product types expressly include certain fund types and funds from certain fund houses. Whether a benefit is a genuine fee discount and whether it has the required promotional connection require judgment.","source_unit_ids":["u8","u13","u14"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The fee-or-charge discount parenthesis qualifies gifts under the selected restriction, including gifts linked to a product type. It does not exempt conduct from other provisions. No actual-distraction test or structured-product exemption is stated for this control. The text does not settle which fees qualify or the treatment of mixed benefits.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u15"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected wording is 'should not', reinforced by 'requirement' and 'will be bound'. It supports a normative restriction, without establishing that every breach is a statutory offence. 'May be considered a gift' leaves classification contingent. The formalized outcome identifies an offer caught by this restriction, not liability or overall compliance.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u24"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The restriction concerns offering gifts in promotion, without a supplied commencement date, deadline or transitional rule. The FAQ date, 2010-09-30, identifies a referenced document and is not established as the control's effective date. Later advertising guidance does not supply that date.","source_unit_ids":["u14","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"Paragraph 3.11 and FAQ question 1 are material unprovided authorities. The packet's external-authorities.23ec46 dependency has no source hash. Statutory, Handbook and advertising provisions remain separate contextual dependencies; their full content or current versions cannot be inferred from the extracts.","source_unit_ids":["u7","u10","u12","u14","u28","u29","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the selected restatement apply to all investment-product promotions by the defined distributors, or only their SFC-authorised-fund promotions?","What do the applicable version of paragraph 3.11 and the referenced FAQ answer say about actor scope, gifts, product linkage and qualifying discounts?","Which fees or charges can be discounted, and how should a package combining a discount and a separate benefit be divided for assessment?","What commencement date and source versions apply to the conduct under review?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["Each evaluation concerns one identified benefit offer to one client; a campaign requires assessment of every relevant offer.","The actor must be a distributor as defined in u1; the Code's title alone does not expand this actor definition.","The general investment-product wording in u14 determines product scope.","Product-type linkage in the promotion is sufficient; proof of actual distraction is not an additional condition.","Unknown classification or scope facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"}],"distinction":"A defined distributor's non-discount gift promoting a specific investment product outside SFC-authorised funds can be caught. The strongest uncertainty is whether the circular's fund-specific setting limits the otherwise general product wording.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit is offered to a client; actual acceptance or delivery is unnecessary for this offer fact.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift, assessed before applying the express discount exception; an additional return or incentive is not automatically classified as a gift.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within u14's exception; merely including a discount elsewhere in a package is insufficient to establish this fact.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer is made in promoting a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to the client, including promotional linkage to a type such as funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The product or product type to which this benefit's promotion is connected falls within the circular's SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","name":"promotion_concerns_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_offered_to_client has_product_promotion_connection)"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Does paragraph 3.11 confirm the general product scope of this restatement despite the circular's fund-specific subject?"],"statement":"Selected control: general-product gift-offer restriction. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, an identified benefit offered to a client in promoting a specific investment product or a particular product type is caught by the 'should not offer' restriction if it is a gift and is not a qualifying fee-or-charge discount. This includes promotional linkage to a fund type or fund house. The restriction does not depend on the arrangement being a structured product or on demonstrated distraction.","subject":"Whether an identified offer is caught by the selected paragraph-10 gift restriction"},{"assumptions":["Each evaluation concerns one identified benefit offer to one client; a campaign requires assessment of every relevant offer.","The actor must be a distributor as defined in u1; the Code's title alone does not expand this actor definition.","The circular's SFC-authorised-fund context limits this selected application of the general wording quoted in u14.","Product-type linkage in the promotion is sufficient; proof of actual distraction is not an additional condition.","Unknown classification or scope facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"This circular summarises the Securities and Futures Commission’s (SFC) recent observations of licensed corporations’ practices in offering and promoting SFC-authorised funds.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"when offering or promoting funds, distributors should not offer additional returns","unit_id":"u15"}],"distinction":"The same distributor's gift promoting only a different investment product is outside this selected application, while gifts connected to SFC-authorised funds remain covered. Outside scope does not mean permitted under the full Code. The strongest uncertainty is that u14 itself states no express SFC-authorised-fund limitation.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit is offered to a client; actual acceptance or delivery is unnecessary for this offer fact.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift, assessed before applying the express discount exception; an additional return or incentive is not automatically classified as a gift.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within u14's exception; merely including a discount elsewhere in a package is insufficient to establish this fact.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer is made in promoting a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to the client, including promotional linkage to a type such as funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The product or product type to which this benefit's promotion is connected falls within the circular's SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","name":"promotion_concerns_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_offered_to_client has_product_promotion_connection promotion_concerns_authorised_funds)"},"local_id":"reading_2","questions":["Is the fund-specific context a limit on this circular's selected application, or merely the occasion for restating a broader control?"],"statement":"Selected control: fund-context gift-offer restriction. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, an identified benefit offered to a client in promoting a specific SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of such funds is caught by the 'should not offer' restriction if it is a gift and is not a qualifying fee-or-charge discount. Product-type linkage includes relevant funds offered by certain fund houses. Structured-product status and actual distraction are not additional conditions.","subject":"Whether an identified offer is caught by the selected paragraph-10 gift restriction"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and the circular’s fund-distribution context.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Observed additional features; does not itself classify every feature as a gift.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Standing-instruction services provide surrounding context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Describes marketing practices without limiting the selected control to public campaigns.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Guaranteed-returns heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Identifies the separate statutory regime.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Explains typical guaranteed-return components; gift classification remains judgment-dependent.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Possible structured-product classification belongs to a separate control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Statutory offence, authorisation and exemptions are not formalized as part of the gift control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Disclosure and misleading-impression concerns provide rationale.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies paragraph 3.11 as the selected control’s source.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Gift control remains relevant even absent structured-product classification; incentive classification is conditional.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"Primary text for the gift restriction, discount exception and product connection.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Connects additional returns and incentives to two distinct requirements without imposing an unconditional ban on every incentive.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u15"},{"reason":"Separate dealing-frequency heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u16"},{"reason":"Observed redemption restrictions concern a separate control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Fairness and redemption duties are outside the selected control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u18"},{"reason":"Administrative procedures and best-endeavours expectations do not supply a gift exception.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u19"},{"reason":"Separate marketing heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u20"},{"reason":"Misleading-advertising duties and paragraph 2.3 require separate assessment.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u21"},{"reason":"Advertising-guideline dependency is outside the selected control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u22"},{"reason":"Risk and deposit-comparison restrictions remain separate advertising controls.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u23"},{"reason":"Monitoring and possible regulatory action do not establish a commencement date or automatic sanction.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u24"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u25"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u26"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u27"},{"reason":"Footnote identifies offering-document requirements; full Handbook provision is unavailable.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u28"},{"reason":"Identifies the Code’s title, including licensed and registered persons; full applicability provisions remain unavailable.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u29"},{"reason":"Identifies the FAQ and its issue date, but the answer itself is absent.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u30"},{"reason":"Unspecified evolving advertising supplements cannot be resolved from this packet.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"u31"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The selected control addresses distributors promoting a specific investment product or particular product type to a client. The circular concerns SFC-authorised funds; its opening reference to licensed corporations does not conclusively exclude registered intermediaries. Public advertising, online distribution and guaranteed returns are not necessary triggers.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u14","u29"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Distributors are identified as intermediaries distributing these funds. Gift and discount are not exhaustively defined. Additional returns or incentives may qualify as gifts, rather than necessarily doing so. Product types expressly include certain fund types and funds from certain fund houses.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u8","u13","u14"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The discount parenthesis qualifies gifts under the selected control, including gifts linked to a product type. Whether eligible fees must relate to that promoted product is unresolved. Section 103 authorisation or exemption is not stated to excuse the gift restriction.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u15"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The source states that distributors 'should not' offer gifts and calls this a requirement. The formalizations identify offers caught by that stated restriction; they do not determine a criminal offence, sanction, or overall compliance. 'May be considered a gift' leaves classification unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u24"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"No circular commencement date or transition period is